<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phintias of Acragas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 279 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phintias was tyrant of Acragas, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agrigento">Agrigento</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in the early 3rd century BCE. In the disorder after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agathocles-of-syracuse">Agathocles of Syracuse</a> he extended his power over neighbouring cities, and around 282 BCE he destroyed Gela and moved its people to a new city named after himself, at modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licata">Licata</a>. His harsh rule provoked revolts, and he was defeated by Hicetas of Syracuse.</p></div>
